2026-11-25  Roman Senn  <roman.l.senn@gmail.com>

	session.inputs and session.outputs getters.

	* quickjs-ort.c (js_ort_session_io_info_one,
	js_ort_session_io_info):
	New. SessionGetInputTypeInfo / SessionGetOutputTypeInfo returns an
	OrtTypeInfo* that is released on every path with ReleaseTypeInfo.
	CastTypeInfoToTensorInfo gives a const OrtTensorTypeAndShapeInfo*
	owned by the type info (not released); it is NULL with OK status when
	the value is not a tensor. GetDimensionsCount and GetDimensions fill
	a js_malloc'ed int64_t array that is js_free'd on every path. The
	element type comes from js_ort_types via js_ort_type_by_onnx, or is
	undefined when the type is not in the table (string, float16, ...)
	or the value is not a tensor. A dynamic dimension is -1, a scalar
	is [], non-tensor dims is undefined. A new Array is created each
	read. magic 0 = inputs, 1 = outputs. Released session throws
	Error('session released'); inputNames and outputNames keep working.

	* quickjs-ort.c (js_ort_session_proto_funcs):
	Add JS_CGETSET_MAGIC_DEF for "inputs" and "outputs" with magic 0
	and 1.

	* quickjs-ort.c (js_ort_throw_released):
	New, the Error of a released session, used by run and by the two
	getters.

	The first version from the nemotron harness read the session before
	it was assigned (segmentation fault), released the tensor info that
	belongs to the type info and used it after the type info was gone,
	and released the type info twice on error paths. js_ort_session_io_info_one
	was rewritten: everything is read while the type info lives and it is
	released exactly once. 100000 reads of inputs and outputs keep the
	resident size flat. The test builder wrote empty dimensions (a message
	wrapped twice) and wrong expected values, and skipped the float16 and
	string cases through an undefined variable, all fixed.

	* tests/session-info-test.js:
	New. Builds models as protobuf bytes (helpers from ort-test.js, plus
	a Dimension with dim_param for dynamic dims). makeModel(elemType,
	dimsSpec, opType) where dimsSpec is numbers or strings. Checks: Add
	float32 with ['N', 3] reports [-1, 3] and runs with [2, 3]; int64
	with [4] reports type int64; float16 and string report type
	undefined with dims [2] (loaded if ORT accepts them on this machine);
	scalar reports dims []; two reads give different Arrays with equal
	content, mutation does not affect the other; after release inputs
	and outputs throw 'session released' while inputNames works; 3000
	reads then final check.

	* doc/native/ort.md (Session table):
	Move session.inputs and session.outputs from Planned to Session with
	semantics: type undefined for unnamed element type or non-tensor,
	dims undefined for non-tensor, dynamic dimension -1.

	* doc/native/ort.md (Planned table):
	Remove the inputs/outputs line.

	* TODO.md (item 1):
	Delete the words "inputs/outputs (name, element type, dims)", keep
	wrapped at about 120 columns.

