2026-11-26  Roman Senn  <roman.l.senn@gmail.com>

	Case 4 groundwork: an STK patch, a JS mel front end, the dataset
	renderer, the trainer and the JS inference model.

	* nn/synths/stkpatch.js, stkpatch.json:
	Subtractive patch from STK generators (saw/square, detuned saw, sub,
	noise, BiQuad with envelope, ADSR, Echo, JCRev), 18 parameters in a
	spec; render() is deterministic, about 100 ms per 1.2 s note at
	22.05 kHz. FreeVerb was left out: it renders differently on every
	call (uninitialised state), JCRev is stable.

	* nn/synths/params.js, nn/features.js:
	Label normalisation, seeded sampling; radix-2 FFT with tables, a real
	signal power spectrum in one half-size FFT, mel filterbank, log-mel.

	* tools/render-dataset.js, nn/nnw.py:
	Writes features, labels and pitch as .nnw, per-example seeds so a
	shard can be regenerated; nnw.py reads them in numpy.

	* train/synth-params.py, nn/models/synth-params.js:
	Conv1d x3 and MLP on log-mel plus pitch; JS inference with the same
	layer names, tests/synth-params-test.js compares it with PyTorch.

	* tests/nn-features-test.js:
	rfftPower against a DFT, mel band of a 1 kHz sine, label roundtrip.

2026-11-26  Roman Senn  <roman.l.senn@gmail.com>

	Fix the reverb in the STK patch, which corrupted half of the dataset.

	* nn/synths/stkpatch.js:
	JCRev gave NaN and levels of several hundred dB when it processed a
	mono StkFrames buffer (it is a stereo effect), which made the first
	validation loss NaN. The reverb now ticks per sample and folds the
	stereo output to mono; render() throws on a non-finite sample. The
	dataset was rendered again.

2026-11-26  Roman Senn  <roman.l.senn@gmail.com>

	String tensors, execution providers, the Windows model path and
	fetching ONNX Runtime from CMake, also for Android and Termux.

	* quickjs-ort.c (js_ort_string_tensor, js_ort_tensor_strings,
	js_ort_tensor_ctor, js_ort_tensor_get_data):
	Tensor('string', Array, dims). ONNX Runtime copies the strings, so the
	tensor keeps no reference to the Array; data is a new Array of strings
	on every read. A non-string element, a NUL byte and a length that does
	not match dims throw before anything is created. session.inputs and
	outputs now report 'string' instead of undefined.

	* quickjs-ort.c (js_ort_providers, js_ort_session_providers,
	js_ort_provider_entry, js_ort_provider_append):
	ort.providers lists GetAvailableProviders. options.providers takes
	names or { name, ...options } in priority order (cpu, cuda, xnnpack,
	nnapi, coreml, qnn, openvino); options go to ONNX Runtime as strings.
	CUDA uses its options object. NNAPI has no name in the generic call, so
	OrtSessionOptionsAppendExecutionProvider_Nnapi is looked up with dlsym
	and takes the option flags. A provider that is not in the build throws
	ONNX Runtime's own Error with its code, there is no silent fallback.

	* quickjs-ort.c (js_ort_session_from_file):
	The model path is converted from UTF-8 to wchar_t on Windows, which
	replaces the #error. Compiled with mingw, not run on Windows.

	* CMakeLists.txt:
	${CMAKE_DL_LIBS} for dlsym on glibc before 2.34.

	* cmake/FindONNXRuntime.cmake:
	BUILD_ORT runs tools/fetch-onnxruntime.sh when nothing is found and
	searches again, ORT_VERSION picks the version. ort_runtime_name()
	names the target's runtime (linux-x64, linux-arm64, android-<arch>,
	also on Termux). The copy in third_party/ is chosen by that name, so a
	linux-arm64 or android directory next to the linux-x64 one is no
	longer taken by accident.

	* tools/fetch-onnxruntime.sh:
	Android runtimes from the Maven Central AAR (headers/ and
	jni/<abi>/libonnxruntime.so). Without RUNTIME the machine's own is
	used (uname), which is what Termux needs. The SONAME link is only
	made when the SONAME differs.

	* tests/string-test.js, tests/providers-test.js,
	tests/session-info-test.js, README.md, doc/native/ort.md, TODO.md,
	BUGS:
	New tests (19 and 19 checks), the string case of session-info-test
	now expects 'string'. Docs describe the new surface. A leak check
	(200 against 5000 rounds of every new path under qjsm --dump) shows
	identical object counts. BUGS has init-api-env-failure-leaves-api-set,
	found while reading js_ort_init_api.

